  "lineage": "French electroacoustic-composition tradition descended from Pierre Schaeffer's 1948-onward musique concrète at Studio d'Essai / GRM (Groupe de Recherches Musicales). Acousmatic refers to music heard from loudspeakers without seeing the source, organized through reduced-listening principles. The post-Schaeffer second generation (François Bayle, Bernard Parmegiani, Luc Ferrari, Beatriz Ferreyra) developed the form into a distinct compositional aesthetic.",
